    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-D01",
      "text": "D01\nGive hosts execute and typed control reports\nSTATED\n\nHosts supply environment, executor factory + module URL, readiness probe, and classified requests. The client returns outpu",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-D02",
      "text": "D02\nKeep declarations free of Node types\nSTATED\n\nThe façade dynamically loads its Node runtime during construction. Portable declarations do not make execution browser-compatible.\n",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-D03",
      "text": "D03\nPackage the process and worker around injected execution\nSTATED\n\nThe package owns executable entries and private mechanisms; the host executor still supplies product behavior. ",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "The old route is still connected ↗",
      "href": "#detail-staging",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-D04",
      "text": "D04\nKeep the shipped CLI on its compatibility graph\nSTATED\n\nThe dispatcher and lifecycle registration remain byte-identical to the base. This PR adds the package path; it does not ",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-D05",
      "text": "D05\nFreeze 38 app-local mechanism files\nSTATED\n\nA path-and-content hash freezes the compatibility graph after preparation. It normalizes CRLF; dispatcher, route, and workspace sele",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-D06",
      "text": "D06\nGroup mechanisms by the concern they own\nSTATED\n\nClient, process, registry, transport, execution, delivery, worker, resources, diagnostics, and lifecycle become package folders",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "The first answer ends the search ↗",
      "href": "#detail-routing",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-D07",
      "text": "D07\nUse four ordered, lazy routing guards\nSTATED\n\nRecord present → not starting → version → responsive. Read and observation are memoized; a decision prevents every later guard and",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-D08",
      "text": "D08\nKeep the route and local-execution distinctions\nSTATED\n\nDisabled, absent, starting, or recovering run cold; ready/busy run warm; dead/incompatible fall back. Only absent/fallba",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-D09",
      "text": "D09\nCompose lifecycle once, with a separate status timeout\nSTATED\n\nDisabled blocks start; status and stop still operate. The host supplies the readiness command, which still runs t",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "A missing answer is not permission to replay ↗",
      "href": "#detail-delivery",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-D10",
      "text": "D10\nLet transport retry-safety authorize fallback\nSTATED\n\nA retry-safe warm submission failure gets one local fallback. An uncertain or accepted failure stays warm and produces a c",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-D11",
      "text": "D11\nOwn warm output capture inside the package\nSTATED\n\nEach transfer gets a fresh policy-limited capture, using memory then an OS-temporary spool. The returned output still has rec",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-D12",
      "text": "D12\nOwn failure output and malformed-result cleanup\nSTATED\n\nResource, response-capacity, and incomplete-request failures become stderr + exit 1. A missing output or non-integer exi",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "Who is allowed to act? ↗",
      "href": "#detail-authority",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-D13",
      "text": "D13\nValidate adopted coordinates inside the coordinator\nUNEXPLAINED\n\nThe renamed coordinator takes coordinates, a serving port, a workspace-exists callback, and an explicit clock. ",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-D14",
      "text": "D14\nGive registry startup equality one owner\nSTATED\n\nCallers request named identity/instance/token/PID checks. One predicate compares the requested coordinates; exact-owner cleanup",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-D15",
      "text": "D15\nPin the existing authentication order and exceptions\nUNEXPLAINED\n\nExecution checks protocol/instance before token. Identify/terminate/kill use identity credentials; ping/stop s",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-D16",
      "text": "D16\nUse a daemon-owned clock API\nSTATED\n\nDaemon mechanisms stop using telemetry clocks and raw time sources. Wall time still owns persisted/lifetime deadlines; monotonic time owns ",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-D17",
      "text": "D17\nDefer readiness- and completion-based idle timing\nSTATED\n\nIdle time starts in the constructor and resets at navigation acceptance. Long startup or a long completed turn can exh",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "The witnesses changed too ↗",
      "href": "#detail-witnesses",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-D18",
      "text": "D18\nMove 37 mechanism test files into the daemon package\nSTATED\n\nPackage tests use generic executor fixtures and local helpers, including standalone module fixtures and tsx tooling",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-D19",
      "text": "D19\nNarrow the relocated worker test\nUNEXPLAINED\n\nGeneric readiness replaces the CLI version scenario and drops startup/execution duration assertions. Version rejection returns as ",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-D20",
      "text": "D20\nReplace the mocked CLI entry tests with built-entry evidence\nSTATED\n\nThe CLI entry test file is deleted. New package tests exercise compiled worker, launcher, process initializ",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-D21",
      "text": "D21\nRetire policy-testing exports and their lint guard\nUNEXPLAINED\n\nThe export map becomes root + two side-effect-only entries. Policy helpers move to test folders; the old import ",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-D22",
      "text": "D22\nAdd a clock-ownership scan limited to one folder\nUNEXPLAINED\n\nThe new test scans only siblings of lifecycle/daemon-clock.test.ts. Process, registry, worker, and execution folde",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-D23",
      "text": "D23\nDisable parallel execution of package test files\nUNEXPLAINED\n\nThe new Vitest configuration sets fileParallelism: false. No explanation accompanies this choice.\n\nreason + eviden",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "decision-D24",
      "text": "D24\nGive Windows termination a different cleanup assertion\nUNEXPLAINED\n\nThe built-process test permits a retained record and absent termination diagnostic on Windows, then has its ",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
